before:
Put this CSS in the stylesheet for the preceding HTML.

```css
.diagram {
  box-sizing: content-box;
  position: relative;
  width: 320px;
  height: 180px;
  border: 1px solid #777;
}
.marker {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  background: crimson;
}
.pointer {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 80px;
  height: 4px;
  background: navy;
  transform-origin: 0 50%;
  transform: rotate(45deg) translateX(6px);
}
```

The pointer begins near the marked coordinate. Its transform changes the displayed shape after layout has placed it. The border makes the reference area visible.

after:
This rule places the pointer and turns it.
```css
.pointer {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform-origin: 0 50%;
  transform: rotate(45deg) translateX(6px);
}
```
The supplied CSS already gives the pointer its size and color.
